Run the PAM credential stack after a successful lockscreen auth.

pam_gnupg only stashes the passphrase in pam_sm_authenticate; the preset into
gpg-agent happens in pam_sm_setcred. Noctalia calls neither pam_setcred nor
pam_open_session, so the passphrase is discarded when the auth child exits and
unlocking the screen never unlocks the keyring. swaylock calls pam_setcred for
exactly this reason.

--- a/src/auth/pam_authenticator.cpp
+++ b/src/auth/pam_authenticator.cpp
@@ -214,6 +214,13 @@
         rc = acctRc;
       }
     }
+    if (rc == PAM_SUCCESS) {
+      // Give the credential stack a chance to run; pam_gnupg presets the
+      // passphrase it captured during pam_authenticate from pam_sm_setcred.
+      // A failure here is not an authentication failure, so rc is left alone.
+      const int credRc = pam_setcred(pamh.h, PAM_REINITIALIZE_CRED);
+      kLog.debug("pam_setcred rc={} ({})", credRc, pam_strerror(pamh.h, credRc));
+    }
     const char* err = pam_strerror(pamh.h, rc);
     const std::string errStr = err != nullptr ? err : i18n::tr("auth.pam.authentication-failed");
     pamh.lastRc = rc;
